# OpenCode V2 standalone mode keeps per-pane notifications mapped correctly.
#
# The notifier bridge (plugins/notify.ts) runs inside the OpenCode server and its
# only pane signal is that server's own $TMUX_PANE, fixed when the server starts.
# --standalone makes the server a child of the TUI, so one server maps to one
# pane and the value stays correct. The shared background service is one process
# for every session in every pane, holding a single pane id: with N panes, N-1
# sessions notify the wrong pane. That is not staleness a restart fixes, though
# it also goes stale once its original pane closes.
#
# oc2 is a temporary compatibility alias. oc2bg is the deliberate opt-in to the
# shared service, and
# it costs ~864 MB less per pane in exchange for losing per-pane notifications.
alias "oc"="command opencode2"
alias "oc2"="command opencode2"
alias "oc2bg"="OPENCODE2_BACKGROUND_SERVICE=true command opencode2"
